   $q$Which sentence best supports the idea that canceling all outside noise could be unsafe?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"When the two waves meet, they cancel each other out, and the noise becomes much quieter.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"partial-evidence"},{"text":"\"Cancel too much, and a walker might not hear a car horn or a bicycle bell.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Your eardrum feels those changes in pressure, and your brain hears them as sound.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"These sounds repeat in a regular pattern, so the chip can predict them.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Cancel too much, and a walker might not hear a car horn or a bicycle bell."$q$, $q$Missing a car horn or a bicycle bell while walking is a safety risk, so that sentence supports the idea directly. The sentence about waves canceling explains how the headphones work but says nothing about danger.$q$, 'draft', '5926b490-2222-522a-9061-0bf4c852108e')
