values
  ('c24226d2-10d5-5f46-859a-8699fc6e9d97', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-evidence-inference'), null, 'easy',
   $q$According to the passage, when do muscles actually get stronger?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Only on days when the athlete feels no soreness at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"At the moment muscle fibers first develop tiny tears","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"During rest, when the body repairs tiny tears in the fibers","is_correct":true},{"text":"During the hardest part of a long, tiring workout","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$During rest, when the body repairs tiny tears in the fibers$q$, $q$The first paragraph says the body repairs the tears "during rest" and that improvement "happens after the workout, not during it." The tears are the cause of the repair, not the moment of strengthening.$q$, 'draft', 'c4cb6e84-5cb9-5608-acfd-145dea8d4e7f')
