  ('6c00041b-90a9-5ac3-8f3a-24cfef421115', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence best explains why overtraining can keep getting worse?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Some athletes respond by training even harder, which only makes the problem worse.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"These activities keep blood flowing to tired muscles without adding much strain.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"Coaches call this overtraining.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"While a person sleeps, the body releases substances that help rebuild muscle and bone.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Some athletes respond by training even harder, which only makes the problem worse."$q$, $q$This sentence describes a cycle: an athlete feels slower, trains harder, and the problem grows. The other sentences name the problem or describe rest, but none explains why it worsens.$q$, 'draft', 'c4cb6e84-5cb9-5608-acfd-145dea8d4e7f')
