  ('9791e6e7-4336-5662-98a0-363b75f120fe', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-evidence-inference'), null, 'easy',
   $q$According to the passage, how is a conservator's job different from a painter's?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Conservators finish their work faster than painters do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Conservators design new murals for towns to approve.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Conservators only work on walls that face the street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Conservators bring back the original instead of adding ideas.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Conservators bring back the original instead of adding ideas.$q$, $q$The passage says "Instead of adding new ideas, conservators try to bring back what the original artist made." Designing new murals would mean adding new ideas, which is the opposite.$q$, 'draft', '907d3804-cc16-5957-b6c5-115b7eb8ad05')
