   $q$Which evidence best supports the claim that the repainted lighthouse matches the original mural?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The team found traces of red paint and used old photographs as a guide.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Several older residents stood across the street for a long time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"The town hired a team of art conservators to do the work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The team matched each color by mixing small test samples.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The team found traces of red paint and used old photographs as a guide.$q$, $q$Traces of the original paint plus photographs of the mural give two direct sources for how the lighthouse looked. Color testing describes the whole job and does not show the lighthouse itself was based on the original.$q$, 'draft', '907d3804-cc16-5957-b6c5-115b7eb8ad05')
